#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Treat a red nightly as a red main: one issue, fixes first, retries.

    forge-nightly [--dry-run]

Run every five minutes from cron, through forge-cron-run, on the host
of the build check, the Merger and the router (designs/0028). Without
a `nightly` section it does nothing. Each tick reads the newest runs of
`nightly.workflow` on the default branch that were scheduled or
dispatched (`schedule`, `workflow_dispatch`), and judges the newest
completed one it has not judged yet by the jobs named `nightly.job`
(or `<job> (...)`, a matrix's): green when each succeeded, red when
one failed or timed out, and neither (cancelled, say) otherwise.
A judged run whose `nightly.release_jobs` all succeeded published its
builds, red or not, and is kept as `published` (without the key, a
green run is), for forge-router's rule 22 (designs/0040).

**One issue while the nightly is red.** A red run with no issue open
opens one, titled `The nightly is red at <sha>`, labelled
`nightly.labels` and `<labels.owner_prefix><owner>` for each owner of a
failed step. It says, for each failed step, its name, its owner and the
end of its output (colour codes removed, at most 12,000 characters a
step, as the build check's `red_comment` quotes one; less a step when
many failed, so the issue fits), and the commits since the last green
nightly. A step's owner is the agent `nightly.owners` maps its name,
or a glob over names, to; a step it names in no way is
`router.owners.triage`'s. A step's output is the lines of its job's log
stamped between its start and end. Each later red run comments once
with the same detail and adds the labels of new owners; one whose
issue was closed meanwhile (a fix's merge closes it) reopens it. The
first green run comments and closes it. The issue is found again by
its `Nightly: <workflow>` line in the open issues the App opened,
so one an earlier tick opened is found even without this tool's state.

**Fixes go first.** While the issue is open, each tick writes the
numbers of the open pull requests that close it (a closing keyword in
the title, the body or a commit message, by forge-closing-keywords'
rule, or the issue in `closingIssuesReferences`) to its state. With
`nightly.fixes_named` (designs/0048 §4), a pull request also fixes it
when it names the issue (`#N` or its URL, any keyword or none, in its
title, body outside code, or commits), or closes an issue linked with
it: one named by `#N` in a comment on it not written by this tool's
App, or one whose own text names it (a cross-reference).
forge-pr-check, forge-merger and forge-router read them there
(agent_forge/nightly.py) and treat them as if they carried
`labels.urgent`. Only the 100 oldest open pull requests are read.

**Run again by itself until green.** While the nightly is red, a tick
dispatches the workflow on the default branch when no run of it is
queued or in progress and either a pull request that closes the issue
merged after the newest run started, or `retry_hours` (default 3) have
passed since it ended. One it dispatched counts as running until a run
created after the dispatch is seen, or DISPATCH_WAIT has passed. Each
dispatch is a comment on the issue, with the commit and why. With
`nightly.defer_until` (designs/0048 §5), it ends with a `Defer-until:`
line at the run's expected end: now plus the median length of the last
five completed runs, rounded up to the quarter hour, kept in the state
as `dispatched.until`; forge-router's rules 20 and 21 hold the issue
until then, or until a red run ends. A red run that ends before then
says so with `Defer-until:` now, the issue's newest line, so the idle
offer (rule 15) stops holding it too.

**A retry fails fast.** When the workflow's file on the default
branch declares a `workflow_dispatch` input named `first`, a dispatch
passes the failed steps of the last red run there, by name, separated
by commas. A workflow without it is dispatched without inputs.

**Escalation.** While the nightly stays red, `escalate_hours` (default
24 and 48) after the issue was opened, the first messages every
developer agent and the second the project's owner, at `tell_owner`
(default `owner`; a name the relay resolves, or a JID), through the
relay with the Merger's sender (`relay.url`, `relay.token_file`;
`$FORGE_ROUTER_RELAY` overrides the url). Each is a comment on the
issue too, the owner's mentioning her. One nobody took is tried again
on the next tick, and not commented on.

**One lead, an issue per step, a notice** (designs/0051, each off
until set). With `nightly.lead`, an agent, the issue is labelled
`nightly.labels` and her Owner label alone, a later red run adds no
Owner label, its body says she leads, the escalations name her, and a
step `owners` doesn't name is hers, not triage's.
With `nightly.step_issues` as well, each failed step gets an issue of
its own, titled `The nightly's <step> is red at <sha>`, labelled
`nightly.labels` and the Owner label of the step's owner (the lead
when `owners` names none), with the step's output, a link to the
nightly's issue and a `Nightly-step: <workflow> <step>` line by which
it is found again. A later red run comments `Red again at <sha>` on
it, and the nightly's issue then lists the step issues instead of
quoting output. A step issue closes when a later run shows its step
succeeding (one skipped proves nothing), and every one closes at the
first green run. Its Owner label is the issue's own: changed by hand,
it stays. nightly.json lists the open ones as `steps`, for the router.
With `nightly.announce`, a name or a room's JID (one with `@`) the
relay resolves, the run that opens the nightly's issue sends one
notice there, and the green run that closes it another; one the relay
doesn't take is tried again each tick for an hour.

Everything is written as the App named by `nightly.as` (default
`merge.merger`, else `Merger`), with a token minted as forge-app-token
does; it needs Actions (to dispatch), Issues and Pull requests. State
(the issue, the last run judged, the last green and red runs, each
with its start and end, the last run that published its builds, the
fixes, the dispatch and the escalations
done) is kept in
~/.local/state/agent-forge/<project>/nightly/nightly.json, and
`forge-stats` reads `nightly_red_hours` from it. `--dry-run` prints
what it would do and changes nothing, on GitHub, in the state or on
the relay.

From the host's crontab:

    */5 * * * * FORGE_CRON_CHECKOUT=$HOME/widget-cron \\
        $HOME/.local/bin/forge-cron-run forge-nightly

Exit status: 0 done, including while the nightly is red (the issue
says so), and when another tick holds the lock; 2 no configuration,
or GitHub could not be read or refused a write.
"""

import argparse
import base64
import datetime
import fnmatch
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import os
import math
import re
import statistics
import sys
import urllib.error
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request

BIN = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(BIN))
from agent_forge import config, github, locks, nightly, state  # noqa: E402

PROG = "forge-nightly"
DEFAULTS = {"owners": {}, "labels": [], "retry_hours": 3,
            "escalate_hours": [24, 48], "fixes_named": False,
            "defer_until": False}
# The events a nightly run starts from.
EVENTS = ("schedule", "workflow_dispatch")
ACTIVE = ("queued", "in_progress", "waiting", "requested", "pending")
GREEN = ("success",)
RED = ("failure", "timed_out", "startup_failure")
# How long a dispatch counts as running before its run is seen.
DISPATCH_WAIT = datetime.timedelta(minutes=30)
# How much of a step's output is quoted, as the build check's red
# comment quotes it, and how much of every step's together, so the
# issue stays under GitHub's 65,536 characters.
STEP_CHARS = 12000
ALL_STEPS_CHARS = 48000
# How many commits since the last green nightly are listed.
COMMITS_SHOWN = 50
ANSI_RE = re.compile(r"\x1b\[[0-9;?]*[A-Za-z]")
LOG_STAMP_RE = re.compile(
    r"^(\d{4}-\d\d-\d\dT\d\d:\d\d:\d\d)(?:\.\d+)?Z ?")
MARKER = "Nightly: %s"
TITLE = "The nightly is red at %s"
# designs/0051: a step issue's title and the line it is found by.
STEP_TITLE = "The nightly's %s is red at %s"
STEP_MARKER = "Nightly-step: %s %s"
# How long a notice the relay didn't take is tried again.
ANNOUNCE_RETRY = datetime.timedelta(hours=1)
REQUEST_TIMEOUT_S = 60
# `nightly.defer_until` (designs/0048 §5): the expected end of a run is
# its start plus the median length of this many recent runs, rounded up.
DURATION_RUNS = 5
DEFER_ROUND = datetime.timedelta(minutes=15)

OPEN_PRS_QUERY = """
query($o: String!, $r: String!, $n: Int!) {
  repository(owner: $o, name: $r) {
    issue(number: $n) {
      state
      comments(last: 100) { nodes { author { login } body } }
      timelineItems(last: 100, itemTypes: [CROSS_REFERENCED_EVENT]) {
        nodes { ... on CrossReferencedEvent {
          source { ... on Issue { number } } } }
      }
    }
    open: pullRequests(states: OPEN, first: 100,
                       orderBy: {field: CREATED_AT, direction: ASC}) {
      nodes { ...closes }
    }
    merged: pullRequests(states: MERGED, first: 30,
                         orderBy: {field: UPDATED_AT, direction: DESC}) {
      nodes { ...closes mergedAt }
    }
  }
}
fragment closes on PullRequest {
  number title body
  closingIssuesReferences(first: 50) { nodes { number } }
  commits(last: 100) { nodes { commit {
    message parents { totalCount }
    associatedPullRequests(first: 5) { nodes { number } } } } }
}
"""


def own_messages(pr):
    """The messages of pull request `pr`'s own commits (GraphQL): not a
    merge, and in no earlier pull request. A stack's upper layer lists
    every commit of the layers below it, and once they merge (as
    squashes) the default branch's as well, so their "Fixes #N" lines
    made the layer look like a fix of whatever they named: on one
    project a layer high in a stack counted as the red nightly's fix,
    went first as urgent and cut the trains again."""
    number = pr.get("number")
    out = []
    for c in (pr.get("commits") or {}).get("nodes") or ():
        commit = (c or {}).get("commit") or {}
        if ((commit.get("parents") or {}).get("totalCount") or 0) > 1:
            continue
        others = [(n or {}).get("number") for n in (
            (commit.get("associatedPullRequests") or {}).get("nodes")
            or ())]
        if any(isinstance(n, int) and isinstance(number, int)
               and n < number for n in others):
            continue
        out.append(commit.get("message") or "")
    return out


def iso(when):
    return when.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def stamp(when):
    return when.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%MZ")


parse_time = nightly.parse_time


def _load_tool(name):
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(
        name.replace("-", "_"), os.path.join(BIN, name))
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader(loader.name, loader)
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(module)
    return module


def owner_of(step, owners, triage):
    """The agent who owns `step`: `owners`' entry for its name, else the
    first glob that matches it, else `triage`."""
    if step in owners:
        return owners[step]
    for pattern, agent in owners.items():
        if not pattern.startswith("_") and fnmatch.fnmatchcase(step,
                                                               pattern):
            return agent
    return triage


def step_map(saved):
    """nightly.json's `steps` (designs/0051), [{name, issue, owner}], as
    {name: entry}; malformed entries are dropped."""
    return {e["name"]: e for e in saved.get("steps") or ()
            if isinstance(e, dict) and isinstance(e.get("name"), str)
            and isinstance(e.get("issue"), int)}


def step_conclusions(jobs):
    """{step name: [conclusion, ...]} over `jobs`' steps."""
    found = {}
    for job in jobs:
        for step in job.get("steps") or ():
            found.setdefault(step.get("name"), []).append(
                step.get("conclusion"))
    return found


def decisive_jobs(jobs, name):
    """The jobs named `name`, or a matrix's `name (...)`."""
    return [j for j in jobs if j.get("name") == name
            or (j.get("name") or "").startswith(name + " (")]


def run_record(run):
    """What nightly.json keeps of the last green run, and of the last
    run that published its builds. `started` is when the run began, so
    the router can tell which labelled issues' fixes it holds
    (designs/0040)."""
    return {"run": run["id"], "sha": run["head_sha"],
            "started": run.get("run_started_at") or run.get("created_at"),
            "ended": run["updated_at"]}


def published(jobs, release_jobs, got):
    """Whether a run published its builds: each of `release_jobs` (by
    name, or a matrix's `name (...)`) ran and every such job succeeded,
    whatever the deciding jobs said. Without `release_jobs`, only a
    green run counts, as before designs/0040's amendment."""
    if not release_jobs:
        return got == "green"
    for name in release_jobs:
        found = decisive_jobs(jobs, name)
        if not found or any(j.get("conclusion") not in GREEN
                            for j in found):
            return False
    return True


def verdict(jobs):
    """"green", "red" or None (neither, or no job) for the deciding jobs."""
    if not jobs:
        return None
    conclusions = [j.get("conclusion") for j in jobs]
    if any(c in RED for c in conclusions):
        return "red"
    if all(c in GREEN for c in conclusions):
        return "green"
    return None


def failed_steps(jobs):
    """[(job, step)] for each step that failed or timed out, in order."""
    return [(job, step) for job in jobs if job.get("conclusion") in RED
            for step in job.get("steps") or ()
            if step.get("conclusion") in RED]


def step_output(log, step):
    """The lines of a job's `log` stamped within `step`'s start and end
    (to the second), their stamps removed; "" when it has none."""
    try:
        start = parse_time(step["started_at"])
        end = parse_time(step["completed_at"])
    except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError, AttributeError):
        return ""
    lines, inside = [], False
    for line in (log or "").splitlines():
        hit = LOG_STAMP_RE.match(line)
        if hit:
            when = parse_time(hit.group(1) + "Z")
            inside = start <= when <= end
            line = line[hit.end():]
        if inside:
            lines.append(line)
    return "\n".join(lines)


def quote(text, limit):
    """`text` with colour codes removed and only its last `limit`
    characters kept."""
    text = ANSI_RE.sub("", text or "").rstrip()
    if len(text) > limit:
        text = "[…]\n" + text[-limit:]
    return text


def fence(text):
    """A code fence longer than any run of backticks in text."""
    runs = [len(r) for r in re.findall(r"`+", text)]
    return "`" * max([3] + [n + 1 for n in runs])


def declares_first(text):
    """Whether a workflow file declares a `workflow_dispatch` input named
    `first`. Read by indentation, without a YAML parser: the key
    `workflow_dispatch:`, its `inputs:`, and `first:` directly under
    that."""
    dispatch = inputs = child = None
    for raw in (text or "").splitlines():
        line = raw.rstrip()
        if not line.strip() or line.lstrip().startswith("#"):
            continue
        indent = len(line) - len(line.lstrip())
        key = line.strip()
        if inputs is not None and indent <= inputs:
            inputs = None
        if dispatch is not None and indent <= dispatch:
            dispatch = None
        if inputs is not None:
            child = indent if child is None else child
            if indent == child and re.match(r"""^["']?first["']?\s*:""",
                                            key):
                return True
            continue
        if dispatch is not None and re.match(r"^inputs\s*:\s*(#.*)?$", key):
            inputs, child = indent, None
            continue
        if re.match(r"""^["']?workflow_dispatch["']?\s*:""", key):
            dispatch = indent
    return False


def fetch_log(token, repo, job_id):
    """A job's whole log as text, or None. GitHub answers with a redirect
    to storage elsewhere, which is followed without the token."""
    class NoRedirect(urllib.request.HTTPRedirectHandler):
        def redirect_request(self, *args, **kwargs):
            return None

    request = urllib.request.Request(
        "%s/repos/%s/actions/jobs/%d/logs" % (github.api_base(), repo,
                                              job_id),
        headers={"Authorization": "token %s" % token,
                 "Accept": "application/vnd.github+json",
                 "User-Agent": "agent-forge"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.build_opener(NoRedirect).open(
                request, timeout=REQUEST_TIMEOUT_S) as resp:
            return resp.read().decode("utf-8", "replace")
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as err:
        where = err.headers.get("Location") if err.headers else None
        if err.code not in (301, 302, 303, 307, 308) or not where:
            return None
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError):
        return None
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(where, timeout=REQUEST_TIMEOUT_S) as resp:
            return resp.read().decode("utf-8", "replace")
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError):
        return None


class Tick:
    """One tick: the settings, GitHub and what to write."""

    def __init__(self, project, token, now, dry_run, out, err, call, logs,
                 send, send_room=None):
        self.project = project
        self.cfg = dict(DEFAULTS, **project.section("nightly"))
        self.name = self.cfg.get("as") or project.section("merge").get(
            "merger", "Merger")
        self.repo = project.repo
        self.main = project.default_branch
        self.workflow = self.cfg["workflow"]
        self.triage = project.section("router").get("owners", {}).get(
            "triage")
        self.token = token
        self.now = now
        self.dry_run = dry_run
        self.out, self.err = out, err
        self.call = call
        self.logs = logs
        self.send = send
        self.send_room = send_room or send
        self.would = "WOULD " if dry_run else ""
        self.failed = False
        # designs/0051.
        self.lead = self.cfg.get("lead")
        self.step_issues = bool(self.lead) and \
            self.cfg.get("step_issues") is True
        if self.lead:
            # A step `owners` doesn't name is the lead's, not triage's.
            self.triage = self.lead
        self.listed = None
        self.closing = _load_tool("forge-closing-keywords")
        self.closing.configure(project)

    def get(self, path, what):
        status, body = github.rest(self.token, "GET", path, call=self.call)
        if status != 200:
            raise RuntimeError("GitHub answered %s for %s" % (status, what))
        return body

    def write(self, method, path, body, want):
        """(whether GitHub took it, its answer); a dry run takes nothing."""
        if self.dry_run:
            return True, {}
        status, got = github.rest(self.token, method, path, body,
                                  call=self.call)
        if status not in want:
            self.failed = True
            self.err("%s: %s %s refused: HTTP %s %s" % (
                PROG, method, path, status,
                (got or {}).get("message", "") if isinstance(got, dict)
                else ""))
            return False, got
        return True, got

    def comment(self, number, text):
        ok, _ = self.write("POST", "/repos/%s/issues/%d/comments"
                           % (self.repo, number),
                           {"body": text + "\n\n" + self.signature()},
                           (201,))
        return ok

    def signature(self):
        return ("Written by forge-nightly, agent-forge's watch on the "
                "nightly (designs/0028).\n\n— %s" % self.name)

    def owner_label(self, agent):
        prefix = self.project.section("labels").get("owner_prefix",
                                                    "Owner:")
        return prefix + agent

    def url(self, number):
        return "https://github.com/%s/issues/%d" % (self.repo, number)

    def runs(self):
        """The workflow's scheduled and dispatched runs on the default
        branch, newest first."""
        body = self.get("/repos/%s/actions/workflows/%s/runs?branch=%s"
                        "&per_page=30" % (
                            self.repo, urllib.parse.quote(self.workflow),
                            urllib.parse.quote(self.main, safe="")),
                        "the runs of %s" % self.workflow)
        runs = [r for r in (body or {}).get("workflow_runs") or ()
                if r.get("event") in EVENTS]
        return sorted(runs, key=lambda r: (r.get("created_at") or "",
                                           r.get("id") or 0), reverse=True)

    def open_issues(self):
        """The open issues the App opened, oldest first, read once a
        tick."""
        if self.listed is None:
            status, items = github.paged(
                self.token, "/repos/%s/issues?state=open&creator=%s" % (
                    self.repo, urllib.parse.quote(
                        self.project.bot_login(self.name), safe="")),
                call=self.call)
            if status != 200:
                raise RuntimeError("GitHub answered %s for the open issues"
                                   % status)
            self.listed = sorted((i for i in items
                                  if "pull_request" not in i),
                                 key=lambda i: i.get("number", 0))
        return self.listed

    def find_steps(self, saved):
        """designs/0051: keep `saved["steps"]` to the step issues still
        open, {step: {"issue", "owner"}}, finding by their
        `Nightly-step:` line any an earlier tick opened; the owner is
        the issue's Owner label (changed by hand, it stays)."""
        prefix = self.owner_label("")
        head = STEP_MARKER % (self.workflow, "")
        known = step_map(saved)
        steps = {}
        for item in self.open_issues():
            for line in (item.get("body") or "").splitlines():
                if line.startswith(head) and line[len(head):].strip():
                    name = line[len(head):].strip()
                    if name in steps:
                        break
                    owners = [l["name"][len(prefix):] if isinstance(l, dict)
                              else l[len(prefix):]
                              for l in item.get("labels") or ()
                              if (l.get("name") if isinstance(l, dict)
                                  else l or "").startswith(prefix)]
                    steps[name] = {"name": name, "issue": item["number"],
                                   "owner": owners[0] if owners else
                                   (known.get(name) or {}).get("owner")}
                    break
        saved["steps"] = list(steps.values())

    def find_issue(self):
        """The open issue the App opened for this workflow, or None."""
        items = self.open_issues()
        marker = MARKER % self.workflow
        for item in sorted(items, key=lambda i: i.get("number", 0)):
            if "pull_request" not in item and marker in (
                    item.get("body") or "").splitlines():
                return item
        return None

    def red_detail(self, run, jobs):
        """(the steps that failed, by name; their owners; the text that
        says so, for the issue or a comment)."""
        failed = failed_steps(jobs)
        names = []
        for _, step in failed:
            if step["name"] not in names:
                names.append(step["name"])
        owners = []
        for name in names:
            agent = owner_of(name, self.cfg["owners"], self.triage)
            if agent not in owners:
                owners.append(agent)
        lines = ["The nightly (`%s`, job `%s`) is red at %s: [run %s](%s), "
                 "ended %s." % (self.workflow, self.cfg["job"],
                                run["head_sha"][:10], run["id"],
                                run.get("html_url", ""),
                                stamp(parse_time(run["updated_at"])))]
        if not failed:
            lines += ["", "No step failed, so it is %s's: the job itself "
                      "did (%s)." % (self.triage, ", ".join(
                          "%s %s" % (j.get("name"), j.get("conclusion"))
                          for j in jobs))]
            owners = owners or [self.triage]
        else:
            lines += ["", "Failed: %s." % ", ".join(
                "`%s` (%s)" % (n, owner_of(n, self.cfg["owners"],
                                           self.triage)) for n in names)]
        limit = min(STEP_CHARS, ALL_STEPS_CHARS // max(1, len(failed)))
        texts = {}
        for job, step in failed:
            if job["id"] not in texts:
                texts[job["id"]] = self.logs(job["id"])
            log = texts[job["id"]]
            text = quote(step_output(log, step), limit) if log else \
                "(the job's log could not be read)"
            mark = fence(text)
            lines += ["", "**%s**%s, %s's, the end of its output:" % (
                step["name"], " in `%s`" % job["name"]
                if len(jobs) > 1 else "",
                owner_of(step["name"], self.cfg["owners"], self.triage)),
                "", mark, text or "(no output)", mark]
        return names, owners, "\n".join(lines)

    def lead_text(self):
        """designs/0051: what the lead is for, in the nightly's issue."""
        return ("%s leads: she drives the nightly to green, chases the "
                "owners of its steps, takes any step without an owner or "
                "given to the wrong agent, and says here when it is green."
                % self.lead)

    def step_outputs(self, jobs):
        """{step name: (job, step, its output quoted)} for each failed
        step, the first of a name."""
        failed = failed_steps(jobs)
        limit = STEP_CHARS
        texts, found = {}, {}
        for job, step in failed:
            if step["name"] in found:
                continue
            if job["id"] not in texts:
                texts[job["id"]] = self.logs(job["id"])
            log = texts[job["id"]]
            found[step["name"]] = (job, step, quote(step_output(log, step),
                                                    limit) if log else
                                   "(the job's log could not be read)")
        return found

    def steps_red(self, saved, run, jobs, number):
        """designs/0051: for each failed step, open its issue or comment
        on the open one. Returns the lines listing them, for the
        nightly's issue."""
        steps = step_map(saved)
        sha = run["head_sha"]
        where = "[run %s](%s)" % (run["id"], run.get("html_url", ""))
        listed = []
        for name, (job, step, text) in self.step_outputs(jobs).items():
            mark = fence(text)
            output = "\n".join(["**%s**%s, the end of its output:" % (
                name, " in `%s`" % job["name"] if len(jobs) > 1 else ""),
                "", mark, text or "(no output)", mark])
            entry = steps.get(name)
            if entry:
                if not self.comment(entry["issue"], "Red again at %s: %s."
                                    "\n\n%s" % (sha[:10], where, output)):
                    return None
                self.out("%sCOMMENT #%d: %s red again at %s" % (
                    self.would, entry["issue"], name, sha[:10]))
            else:
                owner = owner_of(name, self.cfg["owners"], self.triage)
                title = STEP_TITLE % (name, sha[:10])
                ok, got = self.write("POST", "/repos/%s/issues" % self.repo, {
                    "title": title, "body": "\n\n".join([
                        "`%s`, a step of the nightly's job `%s`, is red at "
                        "%s: %s. It is %s's to fix; the nightly as a whole "
                        "is #%s, which %s leads. This closes when a later "
                        "run shows the step succeeding." % (
                            name, self.cfg["job"], sha[:10], where, owner,
                            number, self.lead),
                        output, STEP_MARKER % (self.workflow, name),
                        self.signature()]),
                    "labels": list(self.cfg["labels"])
                    + [self.owner_label(owner)]}, (201,))
                if not ok:
                    return None
                entry = steps[name] = {"name": name,
                                       "issue": (got or {}).get("number"),
                                       "owner": owner}
                saved["steps"] = list(steps.values())
                self.out("%sOPEN %s, for %s" % (self.would, title, owner))
            listed.append("- `%s` (%s): #%s" % (name, entry["owner"],
                                                 entry["issue"]))
        return listed

    def steps_green(self, saved, run, jobs, every):
        """designs/0051: close each open step issue whose step a run
        shows succeeding, or every one (`every`, a green run)."""
        steps = step_map(saved)
        seen = step_conclusions(jobs)
        sha = run["head_sha"]
        for name in list(steps):
            got = seen.get(name) or []
            if not every and not (got and all(c in GREEN for c in got)):
                continue
            number = steps[name]["issue"]
            if not self.comment(number, "`%s` succeeded at %s: [run %s](%s). "
                                "Closing." % (name, sha[:10], run["id"],
                                              run.get("html_url", ""))):
                return False
            ok, _ = self.write("PATCH", "/repos/%s/issues/%d" % (
                self.repo, number), {"state": "closed",
                                     "state_reason": "completed"}, (200,))
            if not ok:
                return False
            del steps[name]
            saved["steps"] = list(steps.values())
            self.out("%sCLOSE #%d: %s succeeded at %s" % (
                self.would, number, name, sha[:10]))
        return True

    def queue_notice(self, saved, text):
        """designs/0051: a notice for `nightly.announce`, sent by
        `announce`."""
        if self.cfg.get("announce"):
            saved["announce"] = {"text": text, "since": iso(self.now)}

    def announce(self, saved):
        """Send the waiting notice to `nightly.announce`; one the relay
        doesn't take is tried again each tick for ANNOUNCE_RETRY."""
        notice = saved.get("announce")
        where = self.cfg.get("announce")
        if not notice or not where:
            saved.pop("announce", None)
            return
        if self.dry_run:
            self.out("WOULD ANNOUNCE to %s: %s" % (where, notice["text"]))
            return
        why = self.send_room(where, "From: forge-nightly\n%s\n"
                             % notice["text"])
        if why is None:
            self.out("ANNOUNCED to %s" % where)
            saved.pop("announce")
            return
        try:
            old = self.now - parse_time(notice["since"]) >= ANNOUNCE_RETRY
        except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError, AttributeError):
            old = True
        self.out("NOT SENT notice to %s: %s; %s" % (
            where, why, "dropped" if old else "tried again next tick"))
        if old:
            saved.pop("announce")

    def commits_since(self, green, sha):
        """Lines listing the commits from the last green nightly to `sha`."""
        if not green or not green.get("sha"):
            return "No green nightly is known to compare with."
        if green["sha"] == sha:
            return "No commits since the last green nightly: the same commit."
        try:
            body = self.get("/repos/%s/compare/%s...%s" % (
                self.repo, green["sha"], sha), "the commits since green")
        except RuntimeError as error:
            return "The commits since the last green nightly (%s) could " \
                "not be read: %s." % (green["sha"][:10], error)
        commits = body.get("commits") or []
        total = body.get("total_commits", len(commits))
        lines = ["Commits since the last green nightly (%s, run %s), %d:"
                 % (green["sha"][:10], green.get("run"), total), ""]
        shown = commits[-COMMITS_SHOWN:]
        if total > len(shown):
            lines.append("- … %d before these" % (total - len(shown)))
        for commit in shown:
            message = ((commit.get("commit") or {}).get("message") or "")
            lines.append("- `%s` %s" % ((commit.get("sha") or "")[:10],
                                        message.split("\n", 1)[0]))
        return "\n".join(lines)

    def explain(self):
        return ("While this is open, a pull request that closes it goes "
                "first: the build check checks it, the Merger merges it "
                "and the router routes it before other work. forge-nightly "
                "runs the nightly again when one merges, or %d h after a "
                "red run ended, and closes this at the first green one."
                % self.cfg["retry_hours"])

    def judge(self, saved, run):
        """Judge one completed run: open, comment on or close the issue."""
        jobs = self.get("/repos/%s/actions/runs/%d/jobs?per_page=100"
                        % (self.repo, run["id"]),
                        "the jobs of run %s" % run["id"]).get("jobs") or []
        every = jobs
        jobs = decisive_jobs(jobs, self.cfg["job"])
        got = verdict(jobs)
        sha = run["head_sha"]
        if published(every, self.cfg.get("release_jobs"), got):
            # Red or green, its builds are out: rule 22 (designs/0040).
            saved["published"] = run_record(run)
            if got != "green":
                self.out("PUBLISHED run %s at %s" % (run["id"], sha[:10]))
        number = saved.get("issue")
        if self.step_issues and not self.steps_green(saved, run, jobs,
                                                     got == "green"):
            return False
        if got == "green":
            self.out("GREEN run %s at %s" % (run["id"], sha[:10]))
            if number is not None:
                text = "The nightly is green at %s: [run %s](%s). Closing." \
                    % (sha[:10], run["id"], run.get("html_url", ""))
                if not self.comment(number, text):
                    return False
                if saved.get("issue_open", True):
                    ok, _ = self.write("PATCH", "/repos/%s/issues/%d" % (
                        self.repo, number), {"state": "closed",
                                             "state_reason": "completed"},
                        (200,))
                    if not ok:
                        return False
                self.out("%sCLOSE #%d: green at %s" % (self.would, number,
                                                       sha[:10]))
                self.queue_notice(saved, "The nightly is green again at %s."
                                  % sha[:10])
            for key in ("issue", "issue_open", "red", "red_since", "opened",
                        "escalated", "dispatched"):
                saved.pop(key, None)
            saved["fixes"] = []
            saved["green"] = run_record(run)
            saved["newest"] = "green"
            return True
        if got != "red":
            self.out("NEITHER run %s at %s: %s" % (
                run["id"], sha[:10], ", ".join(
                    "%s %s" % (j.get("name"), j.get("conclusion"))
                    for j in jobs) or "no job %s" % self.cfg["job"]))
            return True
        names, owners, detail = self.red_detail(run, jobs)
        commits = self.commits_since(saved.get("green"), sha)
        labels = list(self.cfg["labels"]) + [self.owner_label(a)
                                             for a in owners if a]
        if self.lead:
            # designs/0051: her Owner label alone, and none added later.
            labels = list(self.cfg["labels"]) + [self.owner_label(
                self.lead)]
        if self.step_issues and names:
            # The output goes to the step issues; this lists them.
            detail = detail.split("\n\n**", 1)[0]
        self.out("RED run %s at %s: %s" % (run["id"], sha[:10],
                                           ", ".join(names) or "no step"))
        if number is None:
            title = TITLE % sha[:10]
            head = [detail] + ([self.lead_text()] if self.lead else [])
            ok, got_issue = self.write("POST", "/repos/%s/issues" % self.repo, {
                "title": title,
                "body": "\n\n".join(head + [commits, self.explain(),
                                            MARKER % self.workflow,
                                            self.signature()]),
                "labels": labels}, (201,))
            if not ok:
                return False
            saved["issue"] = (got_issue or {}).get("number")
            if self.step_issues and names:
                listed = self.steps_red(saved, run, jobs, saved["issue"])
                if listed is None:
                    return False
                if saved["issue"] is not None:
                    self.comment(saved["issue"], "One issue a red step:\n\n"
                                 + "\n".join(listed))
            self.queue_notice(saved, "The nightly is red at %s: %s. %s%s. "
                              "Merging continues; idle developers, take a "
                              "red step first." % (
                                  sha[:10], ", ".join(
                                      "%s (%s)" % (n, owner_of(
                                          n, self.cfg["owners"], self.triage))
                                      for n in names) or "the job",
                                  "%s leads: " % self.lead if self.lead
                                  else "", self.url(saved["issue"])
                                  if saved["issue"] else "its issue"))
            saved["issue_open"] = True
            saved["opened"] = iso(self.now)
            saved["escalated"] = []
            saved["red_since"] = (saved.get("green") or {}).get(
                "ended") or run["updated_at"]
            self.out("%sOPEN %s, for %s" % (self.would, title,
                                             ", ".join(owners)))
        else:
            if not saved.get("issue_open", True):
                ok, _ = self.write("PATCH", "/repos/%s/issues/%d" % (
                    self.repo, number), {"state": "open"}, (200,))
                if not ok:
                    return False
                saved["issue_open"] = True
                self.out("%sREOPEN #%d" % (self.would, number))
            listed = []
            if self.step_issues and names:
                listed = self.steps_red(saved, run, jobs, number)
                if listed is None:
                    return False
            if not self.comment(number, "Red again.\n\n" + detail + (
                    "\n\nOne issue a red step:\n\n" + "\n".join(listed)
                    if listed else "") + "\n\n" + commits
                    + self.supersede(saved)):
                return False
            if labels and not self.lead:
                ok, _ = self.write("POST", "/repos/%s/issues/%d/labels" % (
                    self.repo, number), {"labels": labels}, (200,))
                if not ok:
                    return False
            self.out("%sCOMMENT #%d: red again at %s" % (self.would, number,
                                                         sha[:10]))
            saved.setdefault("red_since", (saved.get("green") or {}).get(
                "ended") or run["updated_at"])
        saved["red"] = {"run": run["id"], "sha": sha,
                        "started": run.get("run_started_at")
                        or run.get("created_at"),
                        "ended": run["updated_at"], "steps": names}
        saved["newest"] = "red"
        return True

    def supersede(self, saved):
        """With `defer_until`, a line ending the deferral a dispatch wrote
        when its run ended red before then: `Defer-until:` now, the
        newest line, which rule 15 reads (designs/0048 §5)."""
        until = (saved.get("dispatched") or {}).get("until")
        if not self.cfg["defer_until"] or not until:
            return ""
        try:
            if parse_time(until) <= self.now:
                return ""
        except (TypeError, ValueError, AttributeError):
            return ""
        return "\n\nDefer-until: %s" % stamp(self.now)

    def closed_by(self, pr):
        """The issue numbers pull request `pr` (GraphQL) closes: its
        `closingIssuesReferences`, and the closing keywords in its title,
        body (outside code) and commit messages."""
        found = {(n or {}).get("number") for n in (
            (pr.get("closingIssuesReferences") or {}).get("nodes") or ())}
        refs = self.closing.refs
        found |= set(refs(self.closing.blank_code(pr.get("body") or "")))
        found |= set(refs(pr.get("title") or ""))
        for message in own_messages(pr):
            found |= set(refs(message))
        found.discard(None)
        return found

    def closes(self, pr, number):
        """Whether pull request `pr` (GraphQL) closes issue `number`."""
        return number in self.closed_by(pr)

    def names(self, pr, number):
        """Whether pull request `pr` names issue `number` by `#N` or its
        URL, with or without a keyword, in its title, body (outside
        code) or commit messages."""
        pattern = re.compile(r"(?:#|/issues/)%d(?![0-9])" % number)
        texts = [pr.get("title") or "",
                 self.closing.blank_code(pr.get("body") or "")]
        texts += own_messages(pr)
        return any(pattern.search(t) for t in texts)

    def linked(self, issue, number):
        """With `fixes_named`, the issues linked with the nightly's issue
        `number` (GraphQL `issue`): those named by `#N` in comments not
        written by this tool's App (its own list the commits since green,
        whose messages name unrelated numbers), and those whose text
        names it (cross-references from issues)."""
        bot = self.project.bot_login(self.name)
        mine = {bot, bot[:-len("[bot]")] if bot.endswith("[bot]") else bot}
        found = set()
        for c in ((issue.get("comments") or {}).get("nodes") or ()):
            if ((c or {}).get("author") or {}).get("login") in mine:
                continue
            found |= {int(m) for m in re.findall(
                r"#([0-9]+)\b", self.closing.blank_code(
                    (c or {}).get("body") or ""))}
        for item in ((issue.get("timelineItems") or {}).get("nodes") or ()):
            source = (item or {}).get("source") or {}
            if isinstance(source.get("number"), int):
                found.add(source["number"])
        found.discard(number)
        return found

    def fixes_how(self, pr, number, linked, steps=()):
        """How pull request `pr` fixes the nightly's issue `number`, for
        the dispatch comment, or None. Without `fixes_named` only
        closing it counts (designs/0028 §3); with it, naming it or
        closing an issue linked with it does too (designs/0048 §4)."""
        closed = self.closed_by(pr)
        if number in closed:
            return "closes #%d" % number
        if not self.cfg["fixes_named"]:
            return None
        if self.names(pr, number):
            return "names #%d" % number
        for step in sorted(steps):
            # designs/0051: a step issue's fix fixes the nightly.
            if step in closed or self.names(pr, step):
                return "%s #%d, a step of #%d" % (
                    "closes" if step in closed else "names", step, number)
        both = sorted(closed & linked)
        if both:
            return "closes #%d, linked with #%d" % (both[0], number)
        return None

    def fixes(self, number, steps=()):
        """(whether the issue is open, the open pull requests that fix
        it, [(number, mergedAt, how)] of those merged that fix it)."""
        owner, _, name = self.repo.partition("/")
        status, doc = github.graphql(self.token, OPEN_PRS_QUERY, {
            "o": owner, "r": name, "n": number}, call=self.call)
        try:
            repo = doc["data"]["repository"]
            issue = repo["issue"] or {}
            is_open = issue.get("state") == "OPEN"
            open_prs = repo["open"]["nodes"]
            merged = repo["merged"]["nodes"]
        except (KeyError, TypeError):
            raise RuntimeError("GitHub answered %s for the pull requests "
                               "that close #%d" % (status, number)) from None
        linked = self.linked(issue, number) if self.cfg["fixes_named"] \
            else set()
        done = []
        for p in merged:
            how = self.fixes_how(p, number, linked, steps) \
                if p.get("mergedAt") else None
            if how:
                done.append((p["number"], p["mergedAt"], how))
        return (is_open,
                [p["number"] for p in open_prs
                 if self.fixes_how(p, number, linked, steps)], done)

    def expected_end(self, runs):
        """With `defer_until`, when a run started now should end: now
        plus the median length of the last DURATION_RUNS completed runs,
        rounded up to DEFER_ROUND; None without any."""
        lengths = []
        for r in runs:
            if r.get("status") != "completed":
                continue
            try:
                start = parse_time(r.get("run_started_at")
                                   or r["created_at"])
                end = parse_time(r["updated_at"])
            except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError, AttributeError):
                continue
            if end > start:
                lengths.append((end - start).total_seconds())
            if len(lengths) == DURATION_RUNS:
                break
        if not lengths:
            return None
        until = self.now.timestamp() + statistics.median(lengths)
        step = DEFER_ROUND.total_seconds()
        return datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(
            math.ceil(until / step) * step, datetime.timezone.utc)

    def dispatch(self, saved, runs, newest, merged):
        """Dispatch the workflow again when nothing of it runs and a fix
        merged or `retry_hours` have passed."""
        number = saved["issue"]
        active = [r for r in runs if r.get("status") in ACTIVE]
        if active:
            self.out("RUNNING run %s: %s" % (active[0]["id"],
                                            active[0]["status"]))
            return
        sent = saved.get("dispatched") or {}
        if sent.get("at"):
            at = parse_time(sent["at"])
            seen = any(parse_time(r["created_at"]) >= at for r in runs
                       if r.get("created_at"))
            if not seen and self.now - at < DISPATCH_WAIT:
                self.out("DISPATCHED at %s; its run isn't seen yet"
                         % sent["at"])
                return
        if newest is None:
            return
        why = None
        started = parse_time(newest.get("run_started_at")
                             or newest["created_at"])
        for pr, when, how in sorted(merged, key=lambda m: m[1]):
            if parse_time(when) > started:
                why = "#%d, which %s, merged at %s, after run %s " \
                    "started" % (pr, how, stamp(parse_time(when)),
                                 newest["id"])
                break
        retry = datetime.timedelta(hours=self.cfg["retry_hours"])
        if why is None and self.now - parse_time(newest["updated_at"]) \
                >= retry:
            why = "%d h since run %s ended" % (self.cfg["retry_hours"],
                                               newest["id"])
        if why is None:
            return
        head = self.get("/repos/%s/commits/%s" % (
            self.repo, urllib.parse.quote(self.main, safe="")),
            "the head of %s" % self.main).get("sha") or ""
        body = {"ref": self.main}
        steps = (saved.get("red") or {}).get("steps") or []
        first = ""
        if steps and self.takes_first():
            first = ",".join(steps)
            body["inputs"] = {"first": first}
        ok, _ = self.write("POST", "/repos/%s/actions/workflows/%s/"
                           "dispatches" % (self.repo, urllib.parse.quote(
                               self.workflow)), body, (200, 204))
        if not ok:
            return
        self.out("%sDISPATCH %s on %s at %s: %s%s" % (
            self.would, self.workflow, self.main, head[:10], why,
            "; first: %s" % first if first else ""))
        saved["dispatched"] = {"at": iso(self.now), "sha": head, "why": why}
        until = self.expected_end(runs) if self.cfg["defer_until"] else None
        defer = ""
        if until is not None:
            # The router holds the issue until then (designs/0048 §5).
            saved["dispatched"]["until"] = iso(until)
            defer = "\n\nDefer-until: %s" % stamp(until)
        self.comment(number, "Ran the nightly again on `%s` at %s: %s.%s%s"
                     % (self.main, head[:10], why,
                        " The steps that failed last go first: `%s`."
                        % first if first else "", defer))

    def takes_first(self):
        """Whether the workflow's file declares the `first` input."""
        path = ".github/workflows/%s" % self.workflow
        try:
            body = self.get("/repos/%s/contents/%s?ref=%s" % (
                self.repo, path, urllib.parse.quote(self.main, safe="")),
                path)
            text = base64.b64decode(body.get("content") or "").decode(
                "utf-8", "replace")
        except (RuntimeError, ValueError, AttributeError) as error:
            self.err("%s: %s not read, so no `first`: %s" % (PROG, path,
                                                             error))
            return False
        return declares_first(text)

    def escalate(self, saved):
        """Message the developers, then the owner, as the issue ages
        past each of `escalate_hours`."""
        number = saved["issue"]
        try:
            opened = parse_time(saved["opened"])
        except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError, AttributeError):
            return
        done = saved.setdefault("escalated", [])
        hours = (self.now - opened).total_seconds() / 3600
        steps = ", ".join((saved.get("red") or {}).get("steps") or ()) \
            or "the job"
        for level, after in enumerate(self.cfg["escalate_hours"][:2]):
            if level in done or hours < after:
                continue
            if level == 0:
                who = self.project.developers()
                text = ("From: forge-nightly\nThe nightly has been red for "
                        "%d h: %s (%s). A pull request that closes #%d goes "
                        "first: checked, merged and routed before other "
                        "work.%s\n" % (after, self.url(number), steps, number,
                                       " %s leads." % self.lead
                                       if self.lead else ""))
            else:
                who = [self.cfg.get("tell_owner") or self.project.owner]
                text = ("From: forge-nightly\nThe nightly has been red for "
                        "%d h, and the developers were told at %d h: %s "
                        "(%s).%s\n" % (after, self.cfg["escalate_hours"][0],
                                       self.url(number), steps,
                                       " %s leads." % self.lead
                                       if self.lead else ""))
            if self.dry_run:
                self.out("WOULD ESCALATE #%d after %d h to %s" % (
                    number, after, ", ".join(who)))
                continue
            took, missed = [], []
            for name in who:
                why = self.send(name, text)
                (missed if why else took).append(
                    "%s (%s)" % (name, why) if why else name)
            if not took:
                self.out("NOT SENT escalation #%d after %d h: %s; tried "
                         "again next tick" % (number, after,
                                              "; ".join(missed)))
                continue
            note = "Red for %d h: messaged %s through the relay." % (
                after, ", ".join(took))
            if level == 1:
                note = "@%s, the nightly has been red for %d h. %s" % (
                    self.project.owner, after, note)
            if missed:
                note += " Not taken: %s." % "; ".join(missed)
            if self.comment(number, note):
                done.append(level)
                self.out("ESCALATE #%d after %d h: %s" % (number, after,
                                                         ", ".join(took)))


def relay_sender(project, environ):
    """The Merger's relay sender (forge-merger's `relay_sender`)."""
    return _load_tool("forge-merger").relay_sender(project, environ)


def room_sender(project, environ):
    """designs/0051: a sender (where, text) for `nightly.announce`: a
    room's JID (with `@`) through the router's poster to the room, any
    other name as the Merger's sender sends it."""
    router = _load_tool("forge-router")
    router.configure(project, rules=False)
    room = router.make_poster(environ.get("FORGE_ROUTER_RELAY",
                                          router.RELAY),
                              router.relay_token(), kind="room")
    agent = relay_sender(project, environ)

    def send(where, text):
        return room(where, text) if "@" in where else agent(where, text)
    return send


def main(argv=None, out=print, err=None, environ=None, now=None,
         call=github.api_call, sign=github.openssl_sign, mint=None,
         logs=None, sender=None, announcer=None):
    err = err or (lambda line: print(line, file=sys.stderr))
    environ = os.environ if environ is None else environ
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=PROG,
                                     description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])
    parser.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true",
                        help="print what it would do and change nothing")
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
    try:
        checkout = environ.get("FORGE_CRON_CHECKOUT")
        project = config.load(None, environ, cwd=os.path.expanduser(
            checkout) if checkout else None)
    except config.ConfigError as error:
        err("NO-CONFIG: %s" % error)
        return 2
    if "nightly" not in project.data:
        out("%s: no nightly section; nothing is watched" % PROG)
        return 0
    now = now or datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)
    path = nightly.path(project.name, environ, create=True)
    lock = locks.try_lock(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(path), "lock"),
                          str(os.getpid()))
    if lock is None:
        out("BUSY: another tick holds the lock")
        return 0
    with lock:
        saved = state.load(path, {"fixes": []})
        cfg = dict(DEFAULTS, **project.section("nightly"))
        name = cfg.get("as") or project.section("merge").get("merger",
                                                             "Merger")
        try:
            token = (mint or (lambda p, n: github.token(p, n, call, sign)))(
                project, name)
        except github.MintError as error:
            err("%s: skipping this tick: %s" % (PROG, error))
            return 2
        made = []

        def send(who, text):
            # The relay sender is made when an escalation is due, not
            # on every tick.
            if not made:
                made.append((sender or relay_sender)(project, environ))
            return made[0](who, text)
        rooms = []

        def send_room(where, text):
            if not rooms:
                rooms.append((announcer or room_sender)(project, environ))
            return rooms[0](where, text)
        tick = Tick(project, token, now, args.dry_run, out, err, call,
                    logs or (lambda job: fetch_log(token, project.repo, job)),
                    send, send_room)
        try:
            runs = tick.runs()
            done = [r for r in runs if r.get("status") == "completed"]
            newest = done[0] if done else None
            if not saved.get("green"):
                green = next((r for r in done
                              if r.get("conclusion") in GREEN), None)
                if green:
                    saved["green"] = run_record(green)
            if saved.get("issue") is None:
                found = tick.find_issue()
                if found is not None:
                    saved["issue"] = found["number"]
                    saved["issue_open"] = True
                    saved["opened"] = found.get("created_at") or iso(now)
                    saved.setdefault("escalated", [])
            if tick.step_issues:
                tick.find_steps(saved)
            else:
                saved.pop("steps", None)
            if newest is not None and newest["id"] != saved.get("judged"):
                if tick.judge(saved, newest):
                    saved["judged"] = newest["id"]
            tick.announce(saved)
            merged = []
            if saved.get("issue") is not None:
                is_open, fixes, merged = tick.fixes(
                    saved["issue"], [e["issue"] for e in
                                     step_map(saved).values()])
                saved["issue_open"] = is_open
                saved["fixes"] = fixes if is_open else []
                if fixes and is_open:
                    out("FIXES #%d: %s" % (saved["issue"], ", ".join(
                        "#%d" % n for n in fixes)))
                tick.dispatch(saved, runs, newest, merged)
                tick.escalate(saved)
            else:
                saved["fixes"] = []
        except (RuntimeError, KeyError, TypeError, ValueError) as error:
            err("%s: skipping this tick: %s" % (PROG, error))
            return 2
        saved["at"] = iso(now)
        if not args.dry_run:
            state.save(path, saved)
    return 2 if tick.failed else 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
